# Who may sign a change to what installs BOb on a box (O-3, P5 §6.2;
# scripts/verificar-firma-instalacion.sh). Format: ssh-keygen allowed_signers,
# as Bzzz's config/bob/firmantes_imagen, ONE PUBLIC KEY per line, never a
# private one. Only a security key that must be touched to sign is accepted:
#   henry namespaces="bob-install-chain",verify-required sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA...
# (or sk-ecdsa-sha2-nistp256@openssh.com, Secure Enclave included; drop
# verify-required only if the key has no PIN or biometric). CI reads this file
# from main, never from the PR.
# Empty on purpose: until Henry puts his public key here, nothing that installs
# BOb can change.
